# Smritilila's settings. Copy this file to `.env` (it is never committed) and edit. A variable already set in your
# shell wins over the file. Everything here is optional except a database and one way to reach a model.

# (In containers, `docker compose` sets the database address itself and keeps all state in a volume: leave DATABASE_URL and SMRITILILA_DATA_DIR
#  alone, and set only the model below.)

# -- The database: Postgres 17, the version the tests and the containers use. `python scripts/serve.py setup` makes it if it is not there.
#    The login below (smritilila / smritilila) is a local default for a throwaway database: choose your own password before anything you care about goes in it.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://smritilila:smritilila@localhost:5432/smritilila

# -- A model, wired in by you. Every pulse of a world is a call to a model, so nothing acts without one; Smritilila includes none.
#    The narration costs money on a hosted service (each pulse is one call, with a long prompt) and time on a local one.
#
# A model served on this machine or your network, or by a hosted service, at any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (Ollama, vLLM, llama.cpp's server, LM Studio):
# SMRITILILA_LOCAL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# SMRITILILA_LOCAL_MODEL=<model>              # the id of whatever you serve
# SMRITILILA_LOCAL_API_KEY=                   # only if your server asks for one
# SMRITILILA_LOCAL_TIMEOUT=600                # seconds a call may take; a populated scene on modest hardware is slow
#
# Another backend is a module `<name>_provider.py` in src/smritilila/llm/ that registers a provider (see llm/providers.py). With more than one configured:
# SMRITILILA_PRIMARY_PROVIDER=<name>          # which is asked first
# SMRITILILA_ROTATE_SHARE=0                   # the share of the narration sent to the second instead (0 to 1; 0 means only when the first fails)

# -- Where state is kept (the list of worlds, witness logs, backups, the builder's conversations). Unset: the repository's own folder.
# SMRITILILA_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/smritilila

# -- Where the server listens. It is the OWNER's server: a request with no identity header is the owner's, so it listens on this
#    machine only. To serve other people, put an authenticating proxy (Cloudflare Access or similar) in front, name your own email
#    in SMRITILILA_OWNERS, and only then set SMRITILILA_ALLOW_REMOTE=1 and SMRITILILA_HOST=0.0.0.0.
# SMRITILILA_HOST=127.0.0.1
# SMRITILILA_PORT=8198
# SMRITILILA_OWNERS=you@example.com
# SMRITILILA_ALLOW_REMOTE=0
#
# -- The Host allow-list. Every request's Host must be this machine (localhost, 127.0.0.1, ::1) or one of these domains (or a subdomain), else it is refused with a 400:
#    it stops another website's page in your own browser reaching the owner's server. Set your own domain here before a tunnel or proxy is put in front.
# SMRITILILA_ALLOWED_HOSTS=example.com        # comma-separated
# SMRITILILA_HOST_GUARD=enforce               # enforce (refuse) | report (log what would be refused and let it through) | off
#
# -- pg_dump, for a world's backups, if it is not on the PATH:
# PG_DUMP_PATH=/usr/lib/postgresql/16/bin/pg_dump
